[nitpick] Similar to other type assertions in this file, consider using a type guard or local variable after the type check to avoid type assertions and leverage TypeScript's type narrowing capabilities.
```suggestion
      const textPart = part;
      return textPart.text.length;
```

Multiple `process.chdir()` calls without proper error handling could leave the process in an unexpected directory if an error occurs between changes. Consider wrapping the publish operations in try-finally blocks to ensure the working directory is restored:

```typescript
for (const [name] of Object.entries(binaries)) {
  const originalDir = process.cwd()
  try {
    process.chdir(`./dist/${name}`)
    if (process.platform !== "win32") {
      await $`chmod 777 -R .`
    }
    await $`bun publish --access public --tag ${Script.channel}`
  } finally {
    process.chdir(originalDir)
  }
}
```

According to the build script for the AUR `fzf` and `ripgrep` are runtime deps. See https://github.com/sst/opencode/blob/f6b3ffaf64f2cb361f940b50029771f8ef12947e/packages/opencode/script/publish.ts#L89

So, I added them to path in `nixpkgs`

```nix
  postInstall = ''
    wrapProgram $out/bin/opencode \
      --prefix PATH : ${
        lib.makeBinPath [
          fzf
          ripgrep
        ]
      }
  '';
```

